WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:06.680
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and things just
got real on Korra this week. There are still

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.269
2 episodes left. There hasn’t been any news
to indicate whether they’re going to post

00:00:09.269 --> 00:00:16.269
those online back to back just like last year
with the Book 2 finale but Janet Varney and

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:21.380
the other voice actors did mention some of
the things that made this year’s finale

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.490
different. So after we get through all the
WTF moments and my episode 11 review I’ll

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:26.190
explain.

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:29.150
If you’re finding me for the first time
I do Korra videos every week. Be sure to subscribe

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:30.630
to get everything. And for those wondering,
when Korra goes off the air I’m going to

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.570
do bonus videos for a little while and then
start doing Star Wars Rebels. That’s probably

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:36.879
going to be a Friday show, so starting in
October when we would normally watch Korra,

00:00:36.879 --> 00:00:39.179
we’ll just be watching that show. Nice and
simple transition.

00:00:39.179 --> 00:00:45.749
Don’t forget still running the korra giveaway.
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber

00:00:45.749 --> 00:00:47.179
and leave a comment on this video.

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:51.359
So let’s go, careful for spoilers if you
haven’t seen the episode yet. Here are my

00:00:51.359 --> 00:00:57.929
top 5 WTF moments from the episode. Starting
with Number 5 - Chaos in Ba Sing Se

00:00:57.929 --> 00:01:01.149
I didn’t expect Zaheer to actually kill
the Earth Queen, but it looks like that’s

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:05.430
what happened. Which is also bad news for
the ending of this episode. But the city is

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:09.110
a complete shit storm now and everyone is
looting.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:12.720
This reminds me of big times in history when
great empires fell. Like the fall of Rome

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:19.720
when the Vandals sacked the city and made
off with some of the Roman Empire’s greatest

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:23.510
treasures. That’s where the term Vandalism
comes from. That was during the decline and

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:27.910
fall of the Roman Empire. After the government
collapsed Europe entered the Dark Ages. Which

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:29.310
was basically the middle ages.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:36.310
It was the period between the fall of Rome
and the Renaissance. Is this the path that

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:40.330
Korra is on? That’s a good question. There
was no Zaheer in real life, no one person

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:43.500
that crushed Rome. It was a long gradual process.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:48.090
The answer to all of that was the Renaissance.
The word renaissance means “Re-birth”.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:52.560
It was a period after the invention of paper
and the metal movable type that creative ideas

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:57.320
were able to spread. It became this big cultural
movement all over Europe that led to a new

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:00.729
age of creative thinking, art, culture and
society.

00:02:00.729 --> 00:02:04.710
So rewind to where we are on Korra. We’re
right at the fall of Ba Sing Se, implying

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:10.799
that the world will enter “the void” so
to speak. A period of chaos from which Zaheer

00:02:10.799 --> 00:02:15.900
is trying to create so that society will re-birth
itself and usher in a new renaissance of spiritual

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:16.420
enlightenment.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:22.599
That’s why I love his character so much,
he’s so crazy but his logic is solid. That’s

00:02:22.599 --> 00:02:26.790
what would happen. People will find a way
to thrive no matter what. The 100 year war

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:31.950
led to the rise of Aang and a new age of peace.
That was a minor version of what Zaheer is

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:37.139
trying to do. He’s trying to burn the field
so that new crops can grow stronger than before.

00:02:37.139 --> 00:02:40.439
We don’t know anything about what’s happening
in Book 4 yet, so there’s no telling how

00:02:40.439 --> 00:02:42.029
much farther his plan will progress.

00:02:42.029 --> 00:02:46.680
There were a few surprises during Mako and
Bolin’s escape from the city. Mostly Grandma.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:50.999
She is glued to her picture of the Earth Queen.
I hope they explain whether that’s because

00:02:50.999 --> 00:02:54.909
she’s just stuck in her ways. Or if she
has some special connection to the Queen.

00:02:54.909 --> 00:02:59.139
It’s possible they made her stubborn just
so that Bolin could have the moment where

00:02:59.139 --> 00:03:01.819
he throws her over his shoulder like a sack
of potatoes. I’ll talk about that more during

00:03:01.819 --> 00:03:01.989
my review.

00:03:01.989 --> 00:03:04.959
moving on to Number 4 - Suyin and the Metal
Bending Clan

00:03:04.959 --> 00:03:09.719
Couple of big red flags here. First, if you’ve
seen my previous Korra videos you know I totally

00:03:09.719 --> 00:03:14.049
don’t trust Suyin. And there’s the possibility
that this clown person in her circus group

00:03:14.049 --> 00:03:14.790
was zaheer.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:19.159
That’s not confirmed or anything but the
minute Suyin said, let’s bring an army of

00:03:19.159 --> 00:03:24.459
highly trained metalbenders all loyal to me.
I felt like Team Korra was headed for disaster.

00:03:24.459 --> 00:03:28.200
Suyin feels like someone who would totally
drink Zaheer’s kool-aide about ushering

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.419
in a new renaissance. Suyin cares not for
the laws of Lin’s world.

00:03:30.419 --> 00:03:34.590
It’s possible she’s totally genuine. I
don’t think she’s going to be evil or

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:39.079
anything. She just seems like a Zaheer apologist.
But you can let me know if you agree.

00:03:39.079 --> 00:03:42.139
If I were Korra or Lin, I just don’t know
that I’d feel comfortable taking a giant

00:03:42.139 --> 00:03:46.709
group of fighters into battle if I wasn’t
positive they were loyal to me instead of

00:03:46.709 --> 00:03:46.999
being loyal to my questionable sister.

00:03:46.999 --> 00:03:51.719
I did really like Suyin’s armor though.
Before all the metal bending artistry this

00:03:51.719 --> 00:03:56.249
season, Lin putting on her armor in the morning
was one of my favorite metal bending sequences.

00:03:56.249 --> 00:03:58.279
Just her getting her Iron Man swerve on.

00:03:58.279 --> 00:04:02.709
Speaking of which, I know a lot of you feel
like Bolin will learn to Lavabend instead

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:06.879
of learning to Metalbend. It seems like if
you could master one difficult form of subbending,

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:10.010
you could master another. They’re both earth
forms.

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:14.029
Usually it’s just a psycho/spiritual thing.
I know major forms of bending are tied to

00:04:14.029 --> 00:04:21.029
lineage but subbending isn’t some midichlorian
bullshit genetics thing.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:26.160
on to Number 3 - Korra Meets with Iroh again

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:30.810
This was a nice surprise, a bit strange with
the timing, but very welcome. Especially that

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:34.860
they paid off the moment with Zuko. I’m
surprised that he would be surprised Iroh

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:38.770
was in the spirit realm. You’d think Zuko
would have reached a level of spirituality

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:42.500
that would allow him to commune with Iroh
but I guess that’s not the case.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:47.880
Korra was actually trying to use Zaheer’s
methods against him. Calling him out in the

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:53.800
spirit realm. In case you missed it, the advice
Iroh gave Korra. About finding things you

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:58.030
were not looking for, was the same advice
he gave to young Zuko when they were hiding

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:02.060
out in Ba Sing Se. I always love it when Mike
and Bryan bring Last Airbender moments into

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:03.200
the new series.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.840
The Iroh moment was a little out of place
but think of it like a vastly shorter version

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:13.020
of the Iroh episode in Book 2. Korra needs
a lesson from Yoda before she flies to the

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:16.070
Death Star to face Darth Vader and the emperor.

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:19.940
And when she did talk with Zuko, it felt like
he was telling her Aang would have died to

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:24.290
protect the airbenders. He backtracked a little
saying Aang had a greater responsibility to

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:29.590
the world. But the alternative is that he
was implying Aang would have killed team Zaheer

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:34.510
if faced with the choice. Even though killing
is one of the greatest taboos of the Air Nation.

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:38.200
Maybe that means Zaheer isn’t a true Airbender?

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:43.940
Okay so shit starting to hit the fan Number
2 - Team Zaheer versus the Air Nation

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:47.840
The animation and fight choreography on the
whole Air Temple part of the episode was so

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:51.920
above and beyond anything else I’d seen
on the series. I really loved the animation

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:55.690
on Avatar Wan’s episodes last year just
because they were so unique, but inside the

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:59.670
normal Korra episodes. This is the new King
of fight scenes.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:03.900
I know I made a star wars reference with Iroh
and yoda earlier, and it only makes sense

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:10.900
that my mind would go to Obi-Wan Kenobi fighting
Darth Vader in Episode 4 when Zaheer and Tenzin

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:12.740
fought.

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:17.500
They gave him the same type of pan away ending
that they gave to the Earth Queen, so if she’s

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:21.380
dead, it seems like they want us to think
Tenzin is dead too. I’ll follow up on that

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:26.960
in a sec. But I was also very happy to see
that they let Kai take on Ming Hua the combustion

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:30.740
bender. I did not expect the downer ending,
so I thought when he took her on he was going

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:33.340
to take down the airship in some super bending
move.

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:36.380
Like when Lin took down the airship in book
1 before Amon blocked her bending abilities.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:40.140
It’s a children’s show, so I understand
why they showed us him surviving and the baby

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:43.650
air bison rescue at the end. I think if they
had cut that scene out the episode as a whole

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:47.640
would have had more dramatic weight. But I
understand the concern. If they had made kids

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:52.360
think that Kai had died Nick probably would
have gotten a million angry letters from the

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:53.700
parents of crying children.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:57.950
I know a lot of the fandom really hates his
character, so no judging. Be honest, would

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:02.470
you have been okay with them killing him.
If mike and bryan had officially let kai die

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:03.250
in the fall.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:06.960
I would have been okay with it. But again,
killing children isn’t something you see

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:11.390
on Korra. At least I can’t remember them
ever killing a child. At least in an explicit

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:16.640
way. Jet from last airbender is one of the
few exceptions. But he wasn’t a little kid,

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:18.870
he was older than everyone on Team Avatar.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:24.220
and more killing my Number 1 WTF moment - Team
Zaheer Kills Tenzin

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:28.270
Can we all agree that the show at least wants
us to think that they killed him. I’m sure

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:31.670
all will be revealed by episode 12. But until
then, given the way things went down with

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:35.360
the Earth Queen, Tenzin has left this mortal
coil.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:38.900
Enter the Void totally feels like a metaphor
for dying now. Since that’s the title of

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:42.840
episode 12, but it’s not the finale, I’m
really curious if Korra is going to have a

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:45.550
major out of body adventure in book 4.

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:49.820
At this point, the best theory I’ve seen
so far is that Zaheer wants Korra to refuse

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:55.700
Raava and Vaatu. That creates some logic issues
based on what happened during book 2. But

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:59.810
if Zaheer has already accomplished his goal
of revolution, what more could he need Korra

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:01.580
for that he couldn’t do himself?

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:08.470
He needs the portals to be open, which they
are. So it has nothing to do with that. He

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:13.600
could be trying to reset things to pre-avatar
wan status. Meaning he has to kill korra while

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:17.530
she’s in the avatar state. That would end
the cycle of the avatar. If that happened

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:22.220
I suppose Raava’s connection would be severed.
I don’t think Raava would cease to exist.

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:28.420
Let me know what you think Zaheer needs Korra
for. But just to explain the Raava Vaatu logic

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:28.770
problem:

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:33.300
During the book 2 finale. Raava was wiped
out, reset to her zero state. Under normal

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:38.000
conditions, she would have re-emerged from
Vaatu in 10,000 years. No matter what story

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:42.190
the show presented in that finale. You can
never kill evil or good.

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:48.000
They are fundamental states of existence.
The terms good and evil are just our subjective

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.840
way of describing to states of existence.
So you can call raava and vaatu something

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:54.700
else, but neither one will ever be completely
destroyed. They just get suppressed for a

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.660
period of 10,000 years.

00:08:56.660 --> 00:09:02.080
In the finale last year, Jinora just forcibly
sped up Raava’s re-emergence. So you can

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:05.050
influence their cycle. But you can’t stop
it.

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:10.290
So I have small issue with the idea that Avatar
Wan “separated” raava and vaatu. If that

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:15.970
were true, then there would have been no part
of raava inside vaatu for Jinora to extract.

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:19.870
That implies that they were never truly separated.
It’s a big problem that I’m trying not

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:23.880
to overthink, but let me know what your opinion
is on the issue of raava and vaatu and if

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:27.010
it has anything to do with the book 3 finale.

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:32.880
Overall I gave this episode an A plus for
not being afraid to kill a beloved character

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:38.320
and for doing it with the most amazing animation
all year. A pluses all around, the Lin Souyin

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:43.250
scenes in the airship kind of dragged a little.
Iroh was a little out of place but overall

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:45.210
everything was amazing.

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:49.270
The only thing I really noticed was how much
they rushed the Korra portion of the episode.

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:53.210
It felt like this was all about the Air Temple
scenes and they just rushed through all the

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:54.700
korra stuff to get to that part.

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:58.880
I really loved the Iroh Zuko Last Airbender
callbacks even if it seems like Zuko is still

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:03.700
a bit of space cadet in his old age. The way
he was presented in the Korra universe was

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:07.740
as the new Iroh. Like he had achieved a certain
level of enlightenment in the years since

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:11.890
the formation of republic city and retiring
as the Fire Lord. I think they just wanted

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:17.800
a funny callback, so for all intents and purposes,
Zuko is Obi-Wan Kenobi just like Tenzin is.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:22.050
Zuko calling out his daughter in the episode
makes me feel like we will definitely see

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:27.000
her in book 4. They wouldn’t go four seasons
teasing a character and not show her. I wonder

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:32.430
why we haven’t seen her yet. It feels like
seeing who she is will reveal some long standing

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:38.430
mystery. Who did Zuko marry? The best theories
I’ve seen are all Mai. But I’m not current

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:45.180
on the comics, and I know the comics revealed
a little about possible Beifong husbands.

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:49.900
Just to explain what Janet Varney and the
cast were saying about the book 3 finale.

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:53.800
They said it would not be a big spiritual
battle like seasons past. Meaning Korra will

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:57.270
probably not have a giant fight with Team
Zaheer. She’s probably going to sacrifice

00:10:57.270 --> 00:11:02.140
herself and literally enter the void of death.
It seems like everyone important is dying

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:02.880
this season.

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:09.740
There is a Korra book 4 that Janet Varney
is the star of, so even if Korra does sacrifice

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:14.150
herself, I don’t think she will stay dead.
Or die completely. That brings up more questions

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:18.470
than it answers. But I’m going to wait till
after episode 12 to speculate further on Book

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:19.290
4.

00:11:19.290 --> 00:11:23.870
In the meantime, congratulations to this week’s
giveaway winner. Li Cheng, you win an amazon

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:26.100
gift card, I’ll message you on your channel
for details

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:30.540
Right now click here for last week’s korra
video and click here to learn all about the

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:31.760
villains in Star Wars Episode 7.

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:37.100
Thanks for watching. see you guys tonight.
High Fives!.

